From: ayazkussan <ayazkussan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:01:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lubot: envanter aktivasyon defterini okur - esik'in on ulasilmaz girdisi baglanir

esik was the one crate in the series whose whole crate-level contract ("a deferral
without an epoch is a TODO; make the deferral auditable") had no reader in the tree:
the inventory printed measurements and never the schedule. It now does: cmd_envanter
loads training/activation.jsonl through a new cli module, parses it through the
Registry's own gates (declare/admit/ratify - the parser refuses earlier with line
numbers, the Registry refuses with reasons), and prints one report line at the
epoch the caller names with --at, defaulting to 0 because the crate keeps no clock
and the inventory must not gain one either.

Each of the ten unreached entries gets a genuine call site, not a doc mention:
with_note/with_flag build the plan, with_why the change, ratify applies ratified_at
lines, live_at/pending_at/earliest_open feed the report, requires_quorum counts the
consensus changes that are due but not live - and Live::is_on plus Change::is_live_at
are cross-checked against each other on every reported change, their disagreement
being an inconsistency line rather than a silent pick.

Baseline consequence under the same rule as 0022: the ten esik lines stopped being
dead, so this patch deletes them (51 to 41, measured by the gate's own scan, rc=0
afterward) and the README test count moves 325 to 328 by recount of the applied
tree. A deliberate miss caught while writing: the ratify test first asserted the
absence of "unratified" in a line that always contains the words as "0 unratified" -
uncompilable here, so it stays recorded as the class of failure cargo would have
caught for free, and the assertion now checks the count text itself.

Not compiled: no Rust toolchain in this sandbox; verification floor is the 39 gates
on the applied tree, brace/field-symmetry read-through against the crate's signatures,
and grep-level proof that every esik call site type-matches its declaration by hand.
